{"id":2773823225884,"type":"artist","name":"The Zombies","artist":null,"year":1961,"weight":15,"info":{"tags":["psychedelic","60s","The Zombies","classic rock","Psychedelic Rock"],"country":"ES","kind":"Group","similar":["Animals","The Zombies","Johnny Rivers","The Move","Los Bravos","Moby Grape","Paul Revere & The Raiders","The Turtles","The Spencer Davis Group","The Beau Brummels"],"disambiguation":"Spanish Band","begin":"1961","img":"https://cdn-images.dzcdn.net/images/artist/b1c1c7bf0e87a34b5ca78a9f08174b33/1000x1000-000000-80-0-0.jpg","bio":"Banda efímera, sólo hizo tres singles y dos LP's. Zombies lo forman Bernardo Bonezzi y un grupo que ya formaban Juanma del Olmo y otros. Se disuelve a finales de los años 80 pero son decisivos a la hora de comprender la revolución musical española de los 80. Aunaban influencias del glam rock (Lou Reed, David Bowie, Eno) y de la new wave (Talking Heads, B-52's).\n\nEl primer LP llamado Extraños Juegos contiene el mayor exito, Groenlandia, tema incluido en todas las recopilaciones del pop español de los 80's"},"works":[{"id":228248765444126,"type":"album","name":"Begin Here","artist":"The Zombies","year":1965,"weight":7,"yt":"g49ckFpRheo","src":"musthear","from":{"books":[],"podcasts":[],"lists":[{"id":200239132687960,"name":"RYM Top — Rock — British Rhythm & Blues","rank":16,"scaruffi":null},{"id":97155353905344,"name":"RYM Top — R&B — Rhythm & Blues","rank":93,"scaruffi":null},{"id":107432201760054,"name":"RYM Top — Rock — Beat","rank":34,"scaruffi":null}],"n_lists":3}},{"id":216924942012540,"type":"song","name":"Tell Her No","artist":"The Zombies","year":1965,"weight":4,"yt":"opUTDQsLUho","src":"charts,singles","from":{"books":[],"podcasts":[],"lists":[{"id":48761518999397,"name":"Billboard Year-End 1965","rank":74,"scaruffi":null},{"id":132335824845498,"name":"Billboard Year-End Hot 100","rank":74,"scaruffi":null}],"n_lists":2}},{"id":88733521067334,"type":"album","name":"Odessey and Oracle","artist":"The Zombies","year":